# tilepattern

- Label: Tile Pattern
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 3
- Parameters: 308 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/tilepattern.html
- Summary (EN): Creates rectangular tiles that form texture patterns such as brick bonds, herringbone or basketweave. It offers predefined pattern types and a Custom Pattern mode for building your own layouts.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud génère des pavages de carreaux (appareillages de briques, chevrons, vannerie) avec un mode Custom Pattern pour dessiner ses propres dispositions.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: reference layer that sets the output image size and metadata.", "pointmask: optional mask that scales the amount of points.", "stamp0: optional scaling input for stamping."]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Pattern Size", "meaning": "Area the tiles must cover. The page says it should usually be the size of the image."}, {"name": "Pattern Type", "meaning": "Selects a predefined bond or pattern, or Custom Pattern."}, {"name": "Mode", "meaning": "In Custom Pattern: Seamless, Tile Count or Tile Size, which control how tile count and size are defined."}, {"name": "Shape Class / Shape", "meaning": "Chooses the shape drawn in each tile (Basic, Marker or Compound)."}, {"name": "Draw As", "meaning": "Filled, Distance, Gradient or Outline."}, {"name": "Tile Value / Background Value", "meaning": "Value inside and outside the shape."}, {"name": "Row Offset / Row Slide Offset", "meaning": "Shifts tiles horizontally, for example to create brick-wall offsets."}, {"name": "Rotate Pattern / Rotate Tile", "meaning": "Rotates the whole pattern or each tile."}, {"name": "Uniform Scale / Horizontal Scale / Vertical Scale / Inset", "meaning": "Controls tile size and edge dilation."}, {"name": "Prune Tiles", "meaning": "Removes tiles by order, threshold, or every Nth row, column or tile."}, {"name": "Split Tiles", "meaning": "Splits tiles iteratively based on a threshold, number of splits and orientation ratio."}]

- Caveats: ["The page does not explain how the pattern is generated internally, so the exact tiling math is not covered.", "Clip to Size only matters when Pattern Size is smaller than the image.", "Turning off Inset can still leave faint lines. The page suggests disabling Anti-Aliasing and setting Shape Edge Filter to 0.", "Changing Seed changes the random variation.", "The Pattern Expression syntax is described with limited examples."]

